Keep the SBR bit reader inside the SBR payload.

A truncated or inconsistent SBR element made the bit readers run past
the payload (ASan heap/global overflows, UBSan shift exponents):
- buf_getbits.cpp: buf_refill() loads zeros once past bufferLen instead
  of reading the stream structure and the decoder state that follow.
- sbr_crc_check.cpp: a one-byte payload gave a negative CRC length and
  the bits left wrapped; the count is now signed and floored at 0.
- check_crc.cpp: a CRC region that is a multiple of MAXCRCSTEP left no
  rest bits, and 1 << -1 is undefined.
- sbr_extract_extended_data.cpp, ps_read_data.cpp: once the PS header
  had read past the extension, the bits left went negative and were
  passed to buf_getbits() as a read size (shift by 45).

Regression input:
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sbr-payload-overrun.bin.

